  "goodToKnow": "Die Schulpflicht is compulsory schooling: in Germany, children must attend school, usually from age six for at least nine or ten years, plus vocational school or further schooling. Unlike in many countries, it's a duty to attend a school, so homeschooling is generally banned; parents can be fined for keeping children home. Schulpflichtig means of school age. It has no plural."
